		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:lopqc5qlyamugbxdujsojdhb/app.bsky.feed.post/3lsiytljbic2w",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/philhawksworth.dev/post/3lsiytljbic2w",
			"author": {
				"name": "Phil Hawksworth",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/philhawksworth.dev",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:lopqc5qlyamugbxdujsojdhb/bafkreig24xocd4zwmwfuqk6bm6z6qxx7wwfov7pmwn4cunlwsdvdhkipsa"
			},
			"date": "2025-06-26T11:16:57.198Z",
			"content": "<p>This hadn't occurred to me as bring derogatory TBH. Is that the issue?</p>\n<p>I guess if you invent Node, and then invent Deno to be \"Node done the way I wish I had done it to start with\" (not 100% a quote from <a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/did:plc:bh4myx375mqjiaxjphg74uay\">@tinyclouds.org</a>, but sorta) then this language would feel about right.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:lopqc5qlyamugbxdujsojdhb/app.bsky.feed.post/3lsiytlxaqs2w",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:lopqc5qlyamugbxdujsojdhb/app.bsky.feed.post/3lsiytljbic2w",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/philhawksworth.dev/post/3lsiytlxaqs2w",
			"author": {
				"name": "Phil Hawksworth",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/philhawksworth.dev",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:lopqc5qlyamugbxdujsojdhb/bafkreig24xocd4zwmwfuqk6bm6z6qxx7wwfov7pmwn4cunlwsdvdhkipsa"
			},
			"date": "2025-06-26T11:16:57.199Z",
			"content": "<p>FWIW, much of the Deno community were keen for a clean break and distinct separation from Node, but then many more asked for greater compatibility to ease adoption and migration.</p>\n<p>I think this wording is intended to represent that. Not throw stones.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:lopqc5qlyamugbxdujsojdhb/app.bsky.feed.post/3lsiyyruk7k2w",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:7g6egal4g5xxyndeeltr5oss/app.bsky.feed.post/3lshocqhez22v",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/philhawksworth.dev/post/3lsiyyruk7k2w",
			"author": {
				"name": "Phil Hawksworth",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/philhawksworth.dev",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:lopqc5qlyamugbxdujsojdhb/bafkreig24xocd4zwmwfuqk6bm6z6qxx7wwfov7pmwn4cunlwsdvdhkipsa"
			},
			"date": "2025-06-26T11:19:51.630Z",
			"content": "<p>I confess this hadn't occurred to me. I read that as meaning you can move to Deno from Node with good compatibility. Feels like standard language inn this context.</p>\n<p>But it's interesting to hear that this ruffles feathers. I don't think shade was intended. Perhaps greater sensitivity is needed here.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:lopqc5qlyamugbxdujsojdhb/app.bsky.feed.post/3lsj3epvkqs2w",
