			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/collinsworth.dev/post/3lsj5wzuyyk22",
			"author": {
				"name": "Josh Collinsworth",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/collinsworth.dev",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:dr7ktxokjqc2suwnook4k73h/bafkreigotpy47tpnxj2sptza4bsjtdebl4dqyfk6ovvrb26prjpytiinjq"
			},
			"date": "2025-06-26T12:48:21.634Z",
			"content": "<p>My understanding is that, while the percentage of overall Node support appears to be a relatively low number, it does indeed represent the vast majority of use cases.</p>\n<p>Similar to how just adding React support to something would be like 0.001% of npm, but would cover like 70% of current use cases.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
